    <string name="privacy_collection">Data collection</string>
    <string name="privacy_collection_body">fidont doesn\'t collect personal data. It has no accounts, ads, or analytics. Android checks your fingerprint or PIN, and fidont never sees them.</string>
    <string name="privacy_storage">Data storage</string>
    <string name="privacy_storage_body">Passkeys and their account names are stored only on this phone. The keys stay in its secure hardware. If you turn on backup, the phone also keeps an encrypted copy of each new key, and only you can export it to a file. Nothing is uploaded or synced.</string>
    <string name="privacy_network">Internet use</string>
    <string name="privacy_network_body">fidont uses the internet only when you scan a QR code. Your phone and the other device then connect through a relay at cable.ahhkeysummo2d.com, operated by z1xus and served through Cloudflare. Messages are end-to-end encrypted, so the relay and Cloudflare can\'t read them. Both can see your IP address and the time of the connection. The relay keeps no logs.</string>
    <string name="privacy_dongle">Dongle</string>
    <string name="privacy_dongle_body">The dongle stores no passkeys. It forwards requests from the computer to this phone over an encrypted Bluetooth link.</string>
